Glyphka

A generative lettering and symbol studio by Plinka.

Run
bun install --frozen-lockfile
bun run dev

Development uses port 8401. The application builds independently of any
other checkout.

Check
bun run check
bun run test:browser
bun run lint
bun run format:check

Oxlint checks TypeScript, promises, JSX, accessibility and engine imports.
ESLint complements it with the official React Hooks and Compiler checks.
Oxfmt owns formatting; bun run format applies it locally.
The full check includes lint and format verification in CI.

Build
bun run build

The static site is generated in dist/.

Lettering
A-Z, digits and . - +. Sixteen visual families. Continuous mutation,
weight, rounding, width, slant, spacing and transparent cutouts.
The die randomizes all geometry, paint and rendering values. Each letter has further drawings
through the More drawings control. Clicking a letter opens its symbol.
Other directions expands on hover/request and stays collapsed initially.
Hover previews are temporary; clicking commits a direction. A back button
returns from a symbol. Discrete changes morph vector paths, while sliders
update directly during a gesture. Wheel/Ctrl+wheel and the toolbar control zoom.

Presets
The disk opens five named local slots. Save, restore and delete designs,
including their rendering settings and mode. Restoring is undoable.

Shapes
Twenty-two starting forms, including superforms, rosettes, organic curves,
spirals and waves. Edit branches, inset, tension, twist and irregularity.
There is no fixed limit of 48 parts. Each generated form remains editable.
Drag to move; corner handles resize; the top handle rotates.
Shift preserves proportions or snaps rotation to 15-degree steps.
Arrow keys move the selected part; Shift increases the step; Delete removes.

3D
The bottom 2D/3D group enables the 3D renderer for
the current lettering, symbol or composition.
Drag to orbit, scroll to zoom. Adjust extrusion, bevel, rotation, material,
side color, outline, lighting, shadows and background in the render panel.
Boolean contour operations preserve vector cutouts in the actual mesh.
Geometry is generated in a worker. Rendering sleeps while the scene is
still and stops when the tab is hidden. Modules and CPU geometry can prewarm
before activation. Switching to 2D pauses and preserves the existing context.
Fixed PBR lighting is baked offline; solid/gradient fills share a shader variant.

Color
Solid fills and editable linear/radial gradients. Drag, add or remove
stops with the Amplo shadcn gradient picker. Live paint updates the SVG
and GPU materials without rebuilding geometry or resizing the canvas. SVG
painting preserves existing masks and paths. A gesture commits once
to history; storage writes remain debounced. Gradients persist locally
and are included in standalone SVG, 2D PNG and 3D PNG exports.

Exports
Standalone SVG paths and masks without fonts. Transparent 2D PNG at 2x.
The 3D PNG captures the current camera, material and lighting.
Ctrl/Cmd+Z undoes; Ctrl/Cmd+Shift+Z or Ctrl/Cmd+Y redoes.
Designs, render settings and custom colors stay in local browser storage.

Stack
React 19, React Compiler, TypeScript, Vite, Bun, Jotai, shadcn/Base UI,
Tailwind CSS, Motion, i18next and Three.js. Fonts are served locally.

Cloudflare
Pages Direct Upload project: glyphka-plinka.
Checks run on main pushes and pull requests. Publishing requires a push
to main by ExtraBinoss with [PUBLISH] in the latest commit message.
All checks must pass. The deployment uses the verified build artifact.
Pull requests and manual check runs do not deploy.

Required repository Actions secrets:
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID

Configuration: wrangler.jsonc and .github/workflows/ci.yml.
No credentials are stored in this repository.

Inspiration
Paul Nicholson's constructions and lettering for Aphex Twin.
The associated lettering is known as Xylem. Glyphka uses its own generated
alphabet and parametric geometry.

https://www.monotype.com/resources/special-aphex-twin-logo
https://www.factmag.com/2017/02/21/aphex-twin-logo-designer-paul-nicholson-shares-blueprints-iconic-design/

Third-party notices are available in public/licenses/NOTICE.txt.

Performance measurements
bun run scripts/benchmark-engine.ts
bun run preview --port 8403
bun run scripts/benchmark-browser.ts

Reports go to ignored artifacts/. Browser measurements use a local production
build and a software GPU; report that environment when comparing results.
Add ?profile to inspect bounded glyphka:* performance entries in DevTools.
The audit and trace artifacts may contain local paths and must stay untracked.

To regenerate the fixed lighting after changing Three.js or the room:
bun build scripts/bake-environment.browser.ts --outfile artifacts/bake-environment.js --format iife
bun run scripts/bake-environment.ts
